6045417] [17592186050827 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186138409 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050827 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186138410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050827 #edb/ref 1031 "Further Factoring of Polynomials Using GCFs" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050827 #edb/ref 1033 2337 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050827 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "69d60d04-3212-57d7-b613-ac51716a407a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054554 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5137" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054554 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve $f(x)=0,$ where $f(x) = \\dfrac{x+1}{x^2-x-2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054554 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f4a45939-a80c-5e3e-bf2f-b3097a42c2ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054554 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x+1}{{x}^{2}-x-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+1}{(x+1)(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x+1)}}{\\cancel{(x+1)}(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the numerator equal to zero, we get $1=0,$ which is a false statement. Therefore, $f(x)=0$ has no solution." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054555 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5139" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054555 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve $f(x)=0,$ where $f(x) = \\dfrac{x^2-4x}{x^2+5x+6}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054555 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bf127b16-01c5-58c9-903a-e00fe349c011" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054555 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we factor $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-4x}{{x}^{2}+5x+6} \\\\  & =\\frac{x(x-4)}{(x+2)(x+3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(x-4) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to $f(x)=0$ are $x=0$ and $x=4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054556 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5142" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054556 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve $f(x)=0$, where $f(x) = \\dfrac{x^3-2x^2-9x+18}{x^2-x-2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054556 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6d6b343f-756f-5d3b-9231-fe7796d85653" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054556 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-9x+18}{{x}^{2}-x-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}(x-2)-9(x-2)}{(x-2)(x+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-2)({x}^{2}-9)}{(x-2)(x+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-2)(x-3)(x+3)}{(x-2)(x+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x-2)}(x-3)(x+3)}{\\cancel{(x-2)}(x+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-3)(x+3)}{x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the numerator equal to zero and solving for $x$ gives\n\n$$\n(x-3)(x+3) = 0 \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x = \\pm3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to $f(x)=0$ are $x=3$ and $x=-3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054566 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5257" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054566 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve $f(x)=0,$ where $f(x) = \\dfrac{2x + 1}{x^2 + x - 6}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054566 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b8371b7c-dfd8-52b3-9c34-00d6814cc5de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054566 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we factor $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{2x+1}{{x}^{2}+x-6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x+1}{(x+3)(x-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+1 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =-1 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to $f(x)=0$ is $x=-\\dfrac{1}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054739 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054739 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049074 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054739 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055163 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054739 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055471 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054739 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 1759218