are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the numerator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)(x-4) & =0 \\\\ x & =-4,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to $g(x)=0$, in ascending order, are $x=-4$ and $x=4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
